    {"id": 10, "type": "manual",
     "desc": "Part (b): a correct response must explain that multiplying out the four factors means taking either the 1 or the x from each one, so the coefficient of x to the k counts the ways of choosing which k of the four factors contribute an x -- that is, the number of k-element subsets of a four-element set. Naming the resulting coefficients 1, 4, 6, 4, 1 is expected but is not on its own enough for full credit; the choosing argument must be there.",
     "slot": "(b) what the coefficients count",
     "skill": "binomial-expansion", "facet": "binomial-expansion",
     "standard": "HSA-APR.C.5", "difficulty": 4, "bloom": "justify"},

